Ladybird keeps the latest 1000 messages that each document’s console
output, up to a total of about 10 MiB, and sends them to a DevTools
client once it starts watching console messages. Gecko’s DevTools server
sends such a client what ConsoleAPIStorage kept: the last 1000 messages
of each window (STORAGE_MAX_EVENTS). V8’s V8ConsoleMessageStorage keeps
at most 1000 messages and 10 MiB of them (maxConsoleMessageCount and
maxConsoleMessageV8Size). And WebKit’s InspectorConsoleAgent keeps 100
messages (maximumConsoleMessages), which its enable() sends to the
frontend. Unlike all three, which keep the logged values themselves,
Ladybird keeps a message’s arguments as text, so a page without DevTools
keeps no logged objects alive.
